              "ansi": "\r\n\u001b[0m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m❯ \u001b[0m\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m\u001b[48;2;55;55;55mI pushed now. Anything outstanding?\u001b[0m\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       \u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[0m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mEdited PR \u001b[0m\u001b[1m\u001b[4m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m#1561\u001b[0m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m, ran \u001b[0m\u001b[1m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m1\u001b[0m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m shell command \u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[0m\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m⏺ \u001b[0mI updated the description of PR #1561 now that the push has landed: https://github.com/getCUJO/labs-data-live/pull/1561. It covers:\r\n  - the new Lens layout and naming;\r\n  - the replication rule;\r\n  - \u001b[0m\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mplatform-lens.groovy\u001b[0m;\r\n  - the new four-step apply order;\r\n  - the CDW findings: no change to cujo-dw, don't add an \u001b[0m\u001b[38;2;177;185;249maccount_sources \u001b[0mentry, and the drift risk tracked in DST-4350.\r\n\r\n  Still outstanding:\r\n  - \u001b[0m\u001b[1mReview and merge. \u001b[0mSquash-merge if you can: the commit \u001b[0m\u001b[38;2;177;185;249m056b0a17 fix(data-warehouse): tag … cost centre 1230 \u001b[0mchanges \u001b[0m\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mscope.yaml\u001b[0m, but that change was later reverted, so the message describes something the branch no longer does.\r\n  - \u001b[0m\u001b[1mPR title. \u001b[0mIt still says \u001b[0m\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mfeat(data-warehouse): …\u001b[0m. Change it to \u001b[0m\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mfeat(lens): … \u001b[0mif you want the title to match the new layout.\r\n  - \u001b[0m\u001b[1mJenkins. \u001b[0mCheck whether the job for \u001b[0m\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mplatform-lens.groovy \u001b[0mgets picked up automatically or needs creating before step 4.\r\n  - \u001b[0m\u001b[1mDeploy in the listed order\u001b[0m, after merging. Step 3 (the replication rule) has to be live before the first export.\r\n  - \u001b[0m\u001b[1mCDW side, outside this repo. \u001b[0mRedshift auto-ingest needs to watch \u001b[0m\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mew1-labs-data-prd-lens/agent/product_provisioning_states/\u001b[0m. Two other open items there: backfilling the history for Rimas and retiring the Redash query.\r\n\r\n  I haven't checked how the new description renders on GitHub.\r\n\r\n\u001b[0m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m✻ Baked for 29s · done 1:31 PM\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[0m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m※ \u001b[0m\u001b[1m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mrecap: \u001b[0m\u001b[3m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mThe goal is to export Lens product_provisioning_states to CDW, and PR #1561 is pushed with its description rewritten. Next, get it reviewed and squash-merged, then deploy in the four-step apply order.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[0m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m❯ \u001b[0m\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m\u001b[48;2;55;55;55mI've updated the title and the description by hand. There are PR comments, have a look\u001b[0m\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m                                                                                                                                                                                    \u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[0m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mRan \u001b[0m\u001b[1m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m2\u001b[0m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m shell commands \u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[0m\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m⏺ \u001b[0mBoth Copilot comments are stale. They point at text in the old PR description, and your current description already covers both. No code change is needed.\r\n\r\n  1. \u001b[0m\u001b[1m\"Replication prefix does not match the documented CDW target\" \u001b[0m(\u001b[0m\u001b[38;2;177;185;249muse_case.yaml:17\u001b[0m, ID 4466912212). The \"documented target\" it quotes, \u001b[0m\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mcujo-labs-data-prd/lens/...\u001b[0m, comes from the old description. The prefix \u001b[0m\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mew1-labs-data-prd-lens/ \u001b[0mis intentional: it is the new\r\n     replication rule's prefix, and the description now names it under \"For review\". What remains real is outside this PR: Redshift auto-ingest in CDW must watch \u001b[0m\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mew1-labs-data-prd-lens/agent/product_provisioning_states/\u001b[0m.\r\n  2. \u001b[0m\u001b[1m\"Deployment instructions omit the Lens pipeline job\" \u001b[0m(\u001b[0m\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mplatform-lens.groovy:12\u001b[0m, ID 4466912293). Step 4 of the current apply order is \u001b[0m\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mplatform-lens.groovy\u001b[0m, and it links labs-jenkins-jobs#154. This was already handled before the comment.\r\n\r\n  Copilot reviewed commit \u001b[0m\u001b[38;2;177;185;249m958770a2 \u001b[0mat 11:34, which is probably before the description was updated, so it saw the old text.\r\n\r\n  The other comments need nothing: the first Copilot review was on the old commit and found no issues, and the Swarmia comment only links the Jira ticket.\r\n\r\n  I haven't replied to or resolved either thread. If you want, I can post a short reply on each, along the lines of \"Intentional; description updated\" and \"Covered in apply order step 4\", and then resolve them.\r\n\r\n\u001b[0m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m✻ Sautéed for 15s · done 1:38 PM\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[0m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m❯ \u001b[0m\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m\u001b[48;2;55;55;55mReply and resolve, then re-request a review from Copilot\u001b[0m\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m                                                                                                                                                                                                                  \u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[0m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mRan \u001b[0m\u001b[1m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m4\u001b[0m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m shell commands \u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\